<title>FINLAND: OKOBANK SEES 5 PCT FINNISH 1997 GDP GROWTH.</title>
<headline>OKOBANK SEES 5 PCT FINNISH 1997 GDP GROWTH.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish GDP growth will</p>
<p>accelerate to five percent this year and slow slightly to 3.5</p>
<p>percent in 1998 while inflation will remain under control,</p>
<p>Finnish cooperative banking group OKO's economists said</p>
<p>in their new forecast on Monday.</p>
<p>Key figures in OKOBANK's March 24, 1997 forecast:</p>
<p>			   1996	 1997	  1998</p>
<p> GDP		     +3.3	   +5	  +3.5</p>
<p> Exports (goods)     +3.8	   +7	    +5</p>
<p> Imports (goods)     +4.5	   +8	    +8</p>
<p> Consumption	   +3.2	 +3.4	  +3.1</p>
<p>  --private	    +3.3	 +3.9	  +3.5</p>
<p>  --public	     +2.9	   +2	    +2</p>
<p> Investment	    +5.5	+14.5	    +8</p>
<p>  --private	    +6.7	  +15	  +7.5</p>
<p>  --public	     +0.1	  +12	    +9</p>
<p> CPI		     +0.6	   +1	  +1.5</p>
<p> Unemployment	  16.3	 14.5	    13</p>
<p> C/A (FIM billion)    +20	+16.5	 +14.5</p>
<p>*Public sector deficit,</p>
<p> pct of GDP	     2.6	  1.6	    1.1</p>
<p>*Public sector gross debt,</p>
<p> pct of GDP	    58.8	   56	    54</p>
<p> 3-mth Helibor	  3.6	 3.25	   3.5</p>
<p>NOTE - *relevant for third stage of economic and monetary</p>
<p>union (EMU), which Finland wants to join from its scheduled</p>
<p>start in 1999.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
